{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":298834,"ns":0,"title":"Affine space","extract":"In mathematics, an affine space is a geometric structure that generalizes some of the properties of Euclidean spaces in such a way that these are independent of the concepts of distance and measure of angles, keeping only the properties related to parallelism and ratio of lengths for parallel line segments. Affine space is the setting for affine geometry.","description":"Euclidean space without distance and angles","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}